'''Noves Tecnologies d'Empreses, S.A.''' (commonly known as '''NTE''') is a Balboan {{w|data center}} infrastructure company headquartered in [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], [[Sant Cristòfor]]. Founded in 2024 by former [[Abyala Telecom]] executive [[Marc Tubau i Ferrer]] and electrical engineer [[Laura Pons i Vives]], the company builds and manages data center facilities across southern [[Abyala]]. NTE is listed on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] under the ticker NTE and has signed infrastructure contracts with [[Kizan Systems]] of [[Okaiken]] to host the company's {{w|tensor processing unit}} clusters outside the Sanese archipelago.

== History ==

=== Founding (2024) ===

Noves Tecnologies d'Empreses was founded in early 2024 by Marc Tubau i Ferrer and Laura Pons i Vives. Tubau had spent over a decade at [[Abyala Telecom]], where he served as senior director of network infrastructure and oversaw the company's data centre operations across its six markets. In that role, he identified a structural gap in southern Abyala's digital infrastructure: while telecom carriers had invested heavily in mobile and broadband networks, the region lacked purpose-built data center capacity comparable to the facilities found in Okaiken, Volisania, or Breisland. Most enterprises in Balboa and neighbouring countries relied on colocation space in converted telecom rooms or overseas providers, with limited local options for high-density compute hosting.

Pons brought a background in electrical engineering and power systems design. She had previously worked on industrial power distribution projects in [[Estret]] province and later specialised in cooling and power redundancy systems for critical facilities. The two founders combined complementary expertise: Tubau's understanding of the regional telecom and enterprise market with Pons's technical knowledge of data center mechanical and electrical systems.

The company was established as a public limited company ({{lang|ca|Societat Anònima}}, S.A.) from inception, with the founders intending to access public capital markets to fund the capital-intensive business of data center construction. Initial seed capital of approximately $15 million was provided by the founders and a small group of early investors, including former Abyala Telecom colleagues and Balboan private investors.

=== Kizan Systems contract (2024) ===

Later in 2024, NTE secured a multi-year infrastructure contract with [[Kizan Systems]], the Okaiken-based semiconductor and artificial intelligence hardware company. Under the agreement, NTE would build and operate data center facilities in Balboa and Potocsí designed to house Kizan's {{w|tensor processing unit}} clusters, providing the Okaiken company with compute infrastructure outside its domestic market. The contract was significant for both parties: Kizan Systems gained a foothold in southern Abyala for its international cloud and AI compute services, while NTE secured an anchor tenant that validated its business model and provided long-term revenue certainty.

The Kizan contract was the catalyst for NTE's accelerated path to public markets. The capital required to construct purpose-built data center facilities — including power infrastructure, cooling systems, and security — exceeded what the company could raise through private channels alone. The founders determined that an initial public offering would provide the most efficient route to funding the construction programme.

=== Initial public offering (2025) ===

NTE completed its initial public offering on the [[Bolsa de Sant Cristòfor]] in mid-2025, raising approximately $120 million through the sale of new shares. The IPO valued the company at approximately $800 million at the offering price. The proceeds were allocated primarily to land acquisition and construction of the company's first two data center facilities — one in [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], Sant Cristòfor, and one in [[Port Vell (Potocsí)|Port Vell]], [[Potocsí]] — as well as to the procurement of power and cooling infrastructure.

The offering was noted for the speed of the company's path to market, approximately 18 months after founding. The Kizan Systems contract was cited in the IPO prospectus as a material factor in the company's investment case, providing contracted revenue that supported the valuation. The stock began trading under the ticker NTE and was well-received by investors seeking exposure to digital infrastructure in the Abyalan growth market.

=== Facility construction and expansion (2025–2026) ===

Following the IPO, NTE commenced construction of its two initial facilities. The Dàrsena Data Center, located in the company's home district of [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], was the first to become operational, entering service in early 2026. The facility was built on a former industrial site near the port, taking advantage of existing high-capacity power connections and fibre optic infrastructure linking Sant Cristòfor to the international submarine cable network. The Port Vell facility, in Potocsí, entered service in mid-2026.

In 2026, NTE announced plans for a third facility in [[Tapuya]], targeting the country's growing enterprise and government demand for domestic data hosting. The company also signed an additional contract with Kizan Systems to expand the hosted TPU capacity at its Dàrsena facility, reflecting growing demand for AI compute services in the Abyalan region.

